      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pelham sits just east of the Flint River at the crossroads of US 19 and State Route 93, giving it a historic transportation hub feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.georgiaencyclopedia.org/articles/counties-cities-neighborhoods/pelham/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town hosts a full‑power television station, WABW‑TV Channel 14, whose UHF tower reaches as far south as Florida.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
