      "source": "https://www.georgiaencyclopedia.org/articles/counties-cities-neighborhoods/pelham/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pelham’s economy has long been rooted in cotton and pecan farming, with vast fields surrounding the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelham%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Pelham General Store, once a superstore for groceries and farm equipment, closed in 1984 but remains a popular landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
